.TH "SOPLOS-PLYMOUTH-MANAGER" "1" "2026-11-17" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-plymouth-manager \- Plymouth boot splash theme manager for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-plymouth-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-plymouth-manager
chooses, previews, installs and removes the Plymouth boot splash themes of
Soplos Linux from a graphical interface. Built with Tauri 2, Rust and Svelte,
it works on Xfce, Plasma and GNOME, with X11 or Wayland, and it rebuilds the
initramfs with
.BR dracut (8)
or with
.BR update-initramfs (8),
whichever the system uses; when both are installed, dracut is used.
.P
It has one window with a gallery of the installed themes, the one in use
marked, and under it the buttons to apply a theme, preview it in a window,
install one from an archive, remove and refresh the list. Several themes can
be selected at once, with Ctrl or Shift click or the box in the corner of a
card, and removed together. Text-only themes cannot be previewed, and the
theme in use cannot be removed. The footer shows the desktop and the display
protocol.
.P
Changes to the system are made through
.BR pkexec (1),
which asks for the password once for each action. A preview opens a nested X
display and takes a picture of the theme, which is saved as
.I preview.png
in the folder of the theme and goes away with it.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English.
.SH OPTIONS
The application has no command-line options.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B F5, Ctrl+R
Refresh the list of themes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Apply the selected theme.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Preview the selected theme.
.TP
.B Ctrl+I
Install a theme from an archive.
.TP
.B Delete
Remove the selected theme.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/plymouth/themes/
Installed Plymouth themes.
.TP
.I /etc/plymouth/plymouthd.conf
Main Plymouth configuration file, where the theme in use is named.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.plymouthmanager.policy
Polkit policy defining the administrator privileges for changes to the system.
